    {
      "description": "**Technique: Bar Gauge Thresholds & Donut Chart Aggregation**\n\nThe **Bar Gauge** applies the same threshold steps as a color gradient across each service bar, making it easy to compare where each service sits relative to SLO boundaries (scaled from 97-100% to amplify differences). The **Donut Chart** aggregates the fleet into status buckets using fixed series colors — useful when the question is *how many* services are impacted, not which specific value they hold. Both panels use reduceOptions to collapse time series into a single representative value per series.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 3,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29
      },
      "id": 12,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### Compare vs. count\n- **Bar gauge** — where each service sits against the SLO bands\n- **Donut** — how *many* services are impacted",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.3.0-36978054224",
      "targets": [],
      "title": "",
      "type": "text"
    },
