    {
      "description": "**Technique: Timeseries with Threshold Bands + Value Mapping Labels**\n\nThis panel uses thresholdsStyle.mode = 'line+area' to render the three status zones as colored background fills — red below 99%, yellow between 99-99.8%, and green above 99.8%. Horizontal lines mark the exact threshold boundaries so their positions are immediately readable on the Y axis.\n\n**Value mappings** (range type) are applied via fieldConfig.defaults to translate numeric values into status labels at every point of contact with the viewer: Y-axis tick labels now read BAU, Warning, and Critical instead of raw percentages. Tooltip on hover shows the status label alongside the series name. Overrides assign each series a thick (3px), high-contrast line color chosen to remain legible against all three colored background zones.\n\nThe Y axis is constrained to 97-100.5% to amplify differences between services that would otherwise appear as near-identical flat lines.",
